title: "OCDF: offline cassava and maize leaf-disease classifiers with a pre-registered cross-source evaluation"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
authors:
  - family-names: Anietie
    given-names: Aniekan Winner
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DevaWinner/ocdf-cassava-maize"
keywords:
  - plant disease detection
  - cassava
  - maize
  - on-device machine learning
  - LiteRT
  - domain shift
  - test-time adaptation
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Compact EfficientNet-B0 classifiers for cassava and maize leaf diseases, converted to
  LiteRT for offline use on phones (7.8 MiB per crop; 20 ms per image on a 2024 phone and
  86 ms on a 2018 phone), released with the complete pipeline, frozen calibration and
  abstention settings, and the records of a pre-registered study of how the models transfer
  across African image sources. Every reported number can be recomputed from the released
  predictions, and every model and decision is tied to a SHA-256 audit trail.
